Here's a minimal API endpoint handling multipart form uploads with images and a description:

```csharp
// Program.cs

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Raise the max request body size (default is ~28MB)
builder.WebHost.ConfigureKestrel(o => o.Limits.MaxRequestBodySize = 50 * 1024 * 1024);

var app = builder.Build();

app.MapPost("/upload", async (HttpRequest request) =>
{
    var form = await request.ReadFormAsync(new FormOptions
    {
        MultipartBodyLengthLimit = 50 * 1024 * 1024
    });

    var description = form["description"].ToString();
    var files = form.Files.GetFiles("images");

    if (files.Count == 0)
        return Results.BadRequest("No images provided.");

    var saved = new List<string>();

    foreach (var file in files)
    {
        // Validate content type
        if (!file.ContentType.StartsWith("image/"))
            return Results.BadRequest($"'{file.FileName}' is not an image.");

        var destPath = Path.Combine("uploads", $"{Guid.NewGuid()}{Path.GetExtension(file.FileName)}");
        Directory.CreateDirectory("uploads");

        await using var stream = File.Create(destPath);
        await file.CopyToAsync(stream);
        saved.Add(destPath);
    }

    return Results.Ok(new { description, fileCount = saved.Count, paths = saved });
})
.DisableAntiforgery();   // needed for anonymous form POSTs without a token

app.Run();
```

**Key points:**

- **`ConfigureKestrel`** — raises the server-level body limit to 50 MB.
- **`FormOptions.MultipartBodyLengthLimit`** — raises the form-parsing limit to match.
- **`form.Files.GetFiles("images")`** — retrieves all files posted under the `images` field name.
- **`form["description"]`** — reads the text field from the same form.
- **`.DisableAntiforgery()`** — required in .NET 8+ for form endpoints without CSRF tokens.

**Test with `curl`:**

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/upload \
  -F "description=My vacation photos" \
  -F "images=@photo1.jpg" \
  -F "images=@photo2.png"
```
